# This app's runtime configuration lives in app.json -> "extra" (read via
# expo-constants), NOT in a .env file. There is normally nothing to put here.
#
# .env / .env.local etc. are gitignored so a value added for local work can't be
# committed by accident. Only copy this file to .env if you actually need to
# override something locally.
#
# The one thing a .env is good for in an Expo app is EXPO_PUBLIC_* vars, which
# Metro inlines into the JS bundle at build time. Anything here ships to the
# client in plain text — never put a secret in it.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.10:3000
# EXPO_PUBLIC_HERE_API_KEY=your-here-platform-api-key
